WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:04.780
Ready?

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.260
Expanding Career and Technical
Education, or CTE, is one of today's most

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:14.190
popular education policy issues. But
who's been taking these courses? CTE

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.690
course taking has seen a 30-year decline.
Business courses are the major driver.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:23.430
Why? Mostly from the drop in typing
classes since the 80s. Take away business,

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.330
and course taking is flat. But there's
more. While traditional vocational

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.750
concentrators and subjects like
agriculture and manufacturing have

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.770
declined a little, new era concentrators —
those in health care or computer science —

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:40.050
have increased dramatically. These two
groups differ notably. On test scores and

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.129
college-going, traditional concentrators
are below average, while new era

00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:50.340
concentrators look average. CTE no longer
fits 80s stereotypes. Concentrators'

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.120
average outcomes have been rising, but is
it because programs are improving, or

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.469
because they're serving more academic
students? For CTE to be successful,

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:02.520
leaders must not only ensure programs
are meeting targeted outcomes, but also

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.170
that they target the students who need
them the most.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.310
Do you agree? Are CTE programs reaching
the students that need them the most?

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.810
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.340
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.200
research and videos from AEI.

